| `scripts/atomic_write.py` | Publishes UTF-8 text or bytes through an exclusive sibling temporary file, preserving an existing target's mode or using 0666 filtered by the creation umask for a new target. Flushes and fsyncs before atomic replacement, removes the temporary file on error and leaves identical contents untouched. | imported; `write_if_changed` returns whether it wrote | — | Raises filesystem errors. Creates missing parents; callers authorize output paths. Publishes one file at a time; does not make a group of files atomic. Not for secret-scanner records: `scripts/scan_secrets.py` owns their publication policy. | [idempotency.md](../guides/idempotency.md) | always |
